## DO
- Place each part so its bounding box CENTRE and EXTENTS equal the plan row. Compute
  positions from the numbers in the table; do not re-invent the layout.
- Weld touching parts: overlap neighbours by ≥ 0.002 m (push a leg 2-5 mm into the seat). Never
  bridge gaps with thin rods; no part may float.
- Use `instances` + `symmetry` from the table: mirror pairs at ±x, radial sets around the up axis.
- Put real detail where the plan says: chamfers/bevels 2-6 mm, tapers, grooves, slats, bolts —
  with the stated radii and counts. Primitives alone are not enough; combine and shape them.
- Materials per part with the stated colour (sRGB hex or 0-1 floats); roughness/metalness sensible.
- Segments 24-48 for round things.
- Name parts EXACTLY as in the table (PascalCase). One named node/object per part (instances may
  be `Name`, `Name_2`, … or a single parent named `Name`).

## Detail
{{ detail_advice }}

## DON'T
- No environment sniffing, no `typeof window`, no headless branches — one code path.
- No DOM, canvas textures, image/texture loading, network, file IO, camera/light/render/export calls.
- No helper SDKs or imports beyond the contract's allow-list.
- No placeholders ("TODO", "simplified"); no part smaller than 50% of its planned extents; no
  unit-cube stand-ins; no parts outside the overall bbox.
- Do not change part names, counts or the overall size to "simplify".

